### Exercise every button setting away from its default

**Severity:** `medium`

The current test leaves the default-on right button unchanged and never exercises the left-button binding. Toggle both controls away from their defaults and back so every binding is covered.

```suggestion
            rmbLock.SetCheck(false);
            Assert.IsFalse(rmbLock.IsChecked);
            rmbLock.SetCheck(true);
            Assert.IsTrue(rmbLock.IsChecked);

            lmbLock.SetCheck(true);
            Assert.IsTrue(lmbLock.IsChecked);
            lmbLock.SetCheck(false);
            Assert.IsFalse(lmbLock.IsChecked);
```

### Set the duration using the slider step size

**Severity:** `medium`

The slider changes in 100 ms increments, while `QuickSetValue` sends one arrow press per integer and therefore clamps this request at the minimum. Start from Home and send six 100 ms steps to reach 800 ms.

```suggestion
            holdDuration.Click();
            holdDuration.SendKeys(Key.Home);
            for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++)
            {
                holdDuration.SendKeys(Key.Right);
            }
```

### Advance the duration by four slider steps

**Severity:** `medium`

Move from 800 ms to 1200 ms with four 100 ms arrow steps instead of 400 key presses.

```suggestion
            for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++)
            {
                holdDuration.SendKeys(Key.Right);
            }
```
